{"day":"2026-10-23","number":14,"rounds":[{"facts":[{"text":"Vince Lombardi, the namesake of the National Football League's Super Bowl trophy, had only a single playoff loss in his coaching career, at the 1960 NFL Championship Game.","sources":[{"title":"Vince Lombardi","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vince_Lombardi"},{"title":"National Football League","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Football_League"},{"title":"Super Bowl","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Super_Bowl"},{"title":"Vince Lombardi Trophy","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vince_Lombardi_Trophy"},{"title":"1960 NFL Championship Game","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1960_NFL_Championship_Game"}]},{"text":"The entrance to 229 West 43rd Street was not locked for 32 years, and The New York Times could not find the key.","sources":[{"title":"229 West 43rd Street","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/229_West_43rd_Street"},{"title":"The New York Times","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times"}]},{"text":"Thomas Jefferson grew Lacinato kale, an heirloom kale also known as Dinosaur kale, in his Monticello garden.","sources":[{"title":"Thomas Jefferson","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Jefferson"},{"title":"Lacinato kale","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lacinato_kale"},{"title":"Kale","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kale"},{"title":"Monticello","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monticello"}]},{"text":"Elsa Schiaparelli prevented Salvador Dalí from adding mayonnaise to her lobster dress.","sources":[{"title":"Elsa Schiaparelli","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elsa_Schiaparelli"},{"title":"Salvador Dalí","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salvador_Dal%C3%AD"},{"title":"Lobster dress","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lobster_dress"}]},{"text":"Rabbits can control their body temperature with their tails.","sources":[{"title":"Rabbit","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rabbit"},{"title":"Thermoregulation","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thermoregulation"}]}],"fake":4,"original":"Rabbits can control their body temperature with their ears.","change":{"kind":"what","old":"their ears","new":"their tails","start":48,"end":58},"difficulty":0.3333333333333333,"nli":0.9924,"fact_ids":["f9242c5c20e1","898a7c7379a1","3df0048f3aa8","db3172e74c56","1c31662b1930"]},{"facts":[{"text":"15th-century heralds attributed a coat of arms to Jesus based on the instruments of the Passion.","sources":[{"title":"Attributed arms","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attributed_arms"},{"title":"Jesus","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jesus"},{"title":"Arma Christi","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arma_Christi"}]},{"text":"David Tennant founded London's Gargoyle Club, with lavish interiors by Henri Matisse, and whose regular patrons included Fred Astaire, Francis Bacon and Lucian Freud.","sources":[{"title":"David Tennant (aristocrat)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Tennant_(aristocrat)"},{"title":"Gargoyle Club","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gargoyle_Club"},{"title":"Henri Matisse","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henri_Matisse"},{"title":"Fred Astaire","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fred_Astaire"},{"title":"Francis Bacon (artist)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Francis_Bacon_(artist)"},{"title":"Lucian Freud","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lucian_Freud"}]},{"text":"The European great raft spider eats small fish and tadpoles.","sources":[{"title":"Europe","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Europe"},{"title":"Great raft spider","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_raft_spider"},{"title":"Fish","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fish"},{"title":"Tadpole","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tadpole"}]},{"text":"\"Fart Proudly\" is an essay about flatulence written by Benjamin Franklin.","sources":[{"title":"A Letter to a Royal Academy","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Letter_to_a_Royal_Academy"},{"title":"Essay","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Essay"},{"title":"Flatulence","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flatulence"},{"title":"Benjamin Franklin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benjamin_Franklin"}]},{"text":"The design of 432 Park Avenue was inspired by a pencil.","sources":[{"title":"432 Park Avenue","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/432_Park_Avenue"}]}],"fake":4,"original":"The design of 432 Park Avenue was inspired by a trash can.","change":{"kind":"what","old":"a trash can","new":"a pencil","start":46,"end":57},"difficulty":0.6666666666666666,"nli":0.9944,"fact_ids":["ec53ea954bbc","0c62c87917f0","80b90158c75d","85ecbe70faba","a024095f6233"]},{"facts":[{"text":"The Singapore Stone, a sandstone slab bearing an undeciphered 13th century inscription, was blown up by the British in 1843 to make way for a fort.","sources":[{"title":"Singapore Stone","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singapore_Stone"},{"title":"Sandstone","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sandstone"},{"title":"Decipherment","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decipherment"},{"title":"British Empire","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_Empire"}]},{"text":"FEMA determines the impact of a storm based on the service at McDonald's.","sources":[{"title":"Federal Emergency Management Agency","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_Emergency_Management_Agency"},{"title":"Waffle House Index","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waffle_House_Index"},{"title":"Waffle House","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waffle_House"}]},{"text":"Nepal's capital Kathmandu only had one restaurant in 1955.","sources":[{"title":"Nepal","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nepal"},{"title":"Kathmandu","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kathmandu"}]},{"text":"The spread of Christianity in Asia is believed to have reached China during the Tang Dynasty, where it was known as the Luminous Religion.","sources":[{"title":"Christianity in Asia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christianity_in_Asia"},{"title":"China","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China"},{"title":"Tang dynasty","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tang_dynasty"}]},{"text":"The Great Wall of China has impacted the process of evolution in plants.","sources":[{"title":"Great Wall of China","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Wall_of_China"},{"title":"Evolution","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evolution"},{"title":"Plant","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plant"}]}],"fake":1,"original":"FEMA determines the impact of a storm based on the service at Waffle House.","change":{"kind":"what","old":"Waffle House","new":"McDonald's","start":62,"end":74},"difficulty":0.6666666666666666,"nli":0.9946,"fact_ids":["c3c250f9a783","542bf37395c9","c5adaae58d02","1a52d0a03b13","e50ab9f1ff8f"]},{"facts":[{"text":"David Bowie's 1999 album Hours was the first by a major artist available for download from the Internet.","sources":[{"title":"David Bowie","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Bowie"},{"title":"Hours (David Bowie album)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hours_(David_Bowie_album)"}]},{"text":"Yanar Dag is a natural fire that burns \"eternally\" on a hillside on the Absheron Peninsula in Azerbaijan.","sources":[{"title":"Yanar Dagh","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yanar_Dagh"},{"title":"Absheron Peninsula","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Absheron_Peninsula"},{"title":"Azerbaijan","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azerbaijan"}]},{"text":"The Curse of Billy Penn is an alleged curse that may explain the failures of Philadelphia, Pennsylvania professional sports teams.","sources":[{"title":"Curse of Billy Penn","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curse_of_Billy_Penn"},{"title":"Curse","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Curse"},{"title":"Philadelphia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philadelphia"}]},{"text":"According to tradition, American spy Anna Strong signalled members of the Culper Ring during the American Revolutionary War with a lantern.","sources":[{"title":"Anna Strong (spy)","url":"https://e